ce was found to cut throughput by roughly 10%; the task is blocked, depending on the multi-threading work.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-47\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-47\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-47\\n\\n**Title**: Async job scheduler for concurrent batch API work\\n\\n**Status**: Blocked\\n\\n**Assignee**: Bob\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-08-18\\n\\n## Activity History\\n\\n- **2026-08-18**: Alice - Task Create (Open)\\n\\n - *Opened the task because an async batch API scheduler is needed for higher throughput.*\\n\\n- **2026-08-25**: Diana - I/O Race Block (Blocked)\\n\\n - *Blocked after finding a concurrent I/O race that cuts throughput by roughly 10%, depending on the multi-threading work.*\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"clickup task ciph 47 sourc id src cu ciph 47 task id ciph 47 titl async job schedul for concurr batch api work status block assigne bob prioriti normal date creat 2026 08 18 descript add an asynchron job schedul to the batch api for higher throughput under concurr load async worker were ad but a concurr i o race wa found to cut throughput by rough 10 the task is block depend on the multi thread work clickup task ciph 47 sourc id src cu ciph 47 task id ciph 47 titl async job schedul for concurr batch api work status block assigne bob prioriti normal date creat 2026 08 18 accept criterion async job schedul process batch api job concurr without a throughput regress concurr i o race condit is resolv current the block issu clickup task ciph 47 sourc id src cu ciph 47 task id ciph 47 titl async job schedul for concurr batch api work status block assigne bob prioriti normal date creat 2026 08 18 descript add an asynchron job schedul to the batch api for higher throughput under concurr load async worker were ad but a concurr i o race wa found to cut throughput by rough 10 the task is block depend on the multi thread work clickup task ciph 47 sourc id src cu ciph 47 task id ciph 47 titl async job schedul for concurr batch api work status block assigne bob prioriti normal date creat 2026 08 18 activ histori 2026 08 18 alic task creat open open the task becaus an async batch api schedul is need for higher throughput 2026 08 25 diana i o race block block block after find a concurr i o race that cut throughput by rough 10 depend on the multi thread work\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e991efae8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-47-Async-Batch-Processing.md\", \"id\": \"cd124151c990e01e\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.31320807892538616, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1519633713219802, \"vector_similarity\": 0.68944573, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-47-Async-Batch-Processing.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e991efae8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-47-Async-Batch-Processing.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-47-Async-Batch-Processing.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1019, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:02:06\", \"token_count\": 519, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-05\\n\\n<table>\\n<thead>\\n<tr>\\n<th style=\\\"text-align: left;\\\">Task</th>\\n<th style=\\\"text-align: left;\\\">Item</th>\\n<th style=\\\"text-align: left;\\\">Status</th>\\n</tr>\\n</thead>\\n<tbody>\\n<tr>\\n<td style=\\\"text-align: left;\\\">T001</td>\\n<td style=\\\"text-align: left;\\\">Core Redaction Engine</td>\\n<td style=\\\"text-align: left;\\\">Completed (2026-06-05)</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td style=\\\"text-align: left;\\\">T002</td>\\n<td style=\\\"text-align: left;\\\">Financial Regex Detection</td>\\n<td style=\\\"text-align: left;\\\">Completed (2026-06-08)</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td style=\\\"text-align: left;\\\">T003</td>\\n<td style=\\\"text-align: left;\\\">Batch CLI</td>\\n<td style=\\\"text-align: left;\\\">Completed (2026-06-12)</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td style=\\\"text-align: left;\\\">T004</td>\\n<td style=\\\"text-align: left;\\\">REST API Endpoints</td>\\n<td style=\\\"text-align: left;\\\">Completed (2026-06-17)</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td style=\\\"text-align: left;\\\">T005</td>\\n<td style=\\\"text-align: left;\\\">Docker Packaging</td>\\n<td style=\\\"text-align: left;\\\"><strong>Active (Reopened)</strong> — reopened 2026-06-25 on image size/CVE review; not yet met</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td style=\\\"text-align: left;\\\">T006</td>\\n<td style=\\\"text-align: left;\\\">Redaction Policy Config</td>\\n<td style=\\\"text-align: left;\\\">Completed (2026-06-22)</td>\\n</tr>\\n<tr>\\n<td style=\\\"text-align: left;\\\">T010</td>\\n<td style=\\\"text-align: left;\\\">Security Audit</td>\\n<td style=\\\"text-align: left;\\\">Completed (2026-07-10)</td>\\n</tr>\\n</tbody>\\n</table>\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 05 tabl thead tr th style text align left task th th style text align left item th th style text align left status th tr thead tbodi tr td style text align left t001 td td style text align left core redact engin td td style text align left complet 2026 06 05 td tr tr td style text align left t002 td td style text align left financi regex detect td td style text align left complet 2026 06 08 td tr tr td style text align left t003 td td style text align left batch cli td td style text align left complet 2026 06 12 td tr tr td style text align left t004 td td style text align left rest api endpoint td td style text align left complet 2026 06 17 td tr tr td style text align left t005 td td style text align left docker packag td td style text align left strong activ reopen strong reopen 2026 06 25 on imag size cve review not yet met td tr tr td style text align left t006 td td style text align left redact polici config td td style text align left complet 2026 06 22 td tr tr td style text align left t010 td td style text align left secur audit td td style text align left complet 2026 07 10 td tr tbodi tabl\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"table\", \"document_id\": \"e9b23eee8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-07-12-Release-Checklist.md\", \"id\": \"f6b236e144e5939b\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2993494006736237, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.11024565667660526, \"vector_similarity\": 0.74059147, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-07-12-Release-Checklist.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9b23eee8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-07-12-Release-Checklist.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-07-12-Release-Checklist.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1077, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:40\", \"token_count\": 704, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-41\\n\\n# Dependency Inventory: License Compliance Audit (Q3) — Reopened\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2041\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-21 (reflects reopen activity through 2026-08-15)\\n\\n## Original Finding: Ghostscript (AGPLv3)\\n\\nThe initial audit flagged `Ghostscript`, used by the `rasterizer` module for PDF-to-image conversion, as AGPLv3-licensed — on the corporate license blacklist because of its viral copyleft terms for any binary distributed to partner sites.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-41\\n\\n# Dependency Inventory: License Compliance Audit (Q3) — Reopened\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2041\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-21 (reflects reopen activity through 2026-08-15)\\n\\n## First Remediation and Reopen\\n\\nThe team swapped in an alternative PDF parser library to replace the Ghostscript dependency, and that swap was initially marked Completed. On follow-up review, however, the replacement library itself turned out to also be AGPL-licensed — the swap solved the specific Ghostscript dependency but reintroduced the same license category problem one layer down. The task was reopened.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-41\\n\\n# Dependency Inventory: License Compliance Audit (Q3) — Reopened\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2041\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-21 (reflects reopen activity through 2026-08-15)\\n\\n## Current Status: Unresolved\\n\\nCharlie is now searching for an Apache 2.0 or MIT-licensed PDF parser alternative that meets the module's rasterization requirements. No suitable replacement has been confirmed yet, so this audit item remains **Active (Reopened)** — not resolved.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-41\\n\\n# Dependency Inventory: License Compliance Audit (Q3) — Reopened\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2041\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-21 (reflects reopen activity through 2026-08-15)\\n\\n## Secondary Open Item\\n\\nTesseract OCR itself is Apache 2.0, but the `eng.traineddata` model files were sourced from a community repository and their training-corpus provenance has not been verified as public-domain/CC0. This remains a separate, lower-priority open item pending Evan's trace of the `tessdata_best` provenance.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 41 depend inventori licens complianc audit q3 reopen owner diana document key doc 2041 last updat 2026 08 21 reflect reopen activ through 2026 08 15 origin find ghostscript agplv3 the initi audit flag ghostscript use by the raster modul for pdf to imag convers a agplv3 licens on the corpor licens blacklist becaus of it viral copyleft term for ani binari distribut to partner site sourc id src gdoc 41 depend inventori licens complianc audit q3 reopen owner diana document key doc 2041 last updat 2026 08 21 reflect reopen activ through 2026 08 15 first remedi and reopen the team swap in an altern pdf parser librari to replac the ghostscript depend and that swap wa initi mark complet on follow up review howev the replac librari itself turn out to also be agpl licens the swap solv the specif ghostscript depend but reintroduc the same licens categori problem one layer down the task wa reopen sourc id src gdoc 41 depend inventori licens complianc audit q3 reopen owner diana document key doc 2041 last updat 2026 08 21 reflect reopen activ through 2026 08 15 current status unresolv charli is now search for an apach 20 or mit licens pdf parser altern that meet the modul s raster requir no suitabl replac ha been confirm yet so this audit item remain activ reopen not resolv sourc id src gdoc 41 depend inventori licens complianc audit q3 reopen owner diana document key doc 2041 last updat 2026 08 21 reflect reopen activ through 2026 08 15 secondari open item tesseract ocr itself is apach 20 but the eng traineddata model file were sourc from a communiti repositori and their train corpus proven ha not been verifi a public domain cc0 this remain a separ lower prioriti open item pend evan s trace of the tessdata _ best proven\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9d4f0568a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-21-License-Compliance-Audit-Report.md\", \"id\": \"039b629d788751dd\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2971086747743287, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.12693274253475526, \"vector_similarity\": 0.69418585, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-21-License-Compliance-Audit-Report.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9d4f0568a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-21-License-Compliance-Audit-Report.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-21-License-Compliance-Audit-Report.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1689, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:12\", \"token_count\": 582, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-50\\n\\n# Queue Design Review: Async Batch Processing — Concurrency Block\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2050\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-04 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-25)\\n\\n## Worker Management Decision\\n\\nRetrospective note on the concurrency block confirmed 2026-08-25. For large-scale redaction jobs, the batch API moved from a synchronous blocking loop to an `asyncio`-driven queue: a single producer walks the file system and pushes document tasks, while a fixed pool of async workers pulls from the queue and orchestrates I/O against the redaction engine, built on top of the already-completed multi-threaded worker pool (T026).\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-50\\n\\n# Queue Design Review: Async Batch Processing — Concurrency Block\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2050\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-04 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-25)\\n\\n## Ordering & Race Risk\\n\\nBecause documents vary widely in size, workers finish out of order. When multiple workers append to the same shared results manifest concurrently, writes can interleave and corrupt the JSON structure.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-50\\n\\n# Queue Design Review: Async Batch Processing — Concurrency Block\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2050\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-04 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-25)\\n\\n## Update: Confirmed I/O Race, Throughput Regression\\n\\nConcurrency testing on 2026-08-25 confirmed the race is real, not just theoretical: under concurrent load, the race condition measurably cuts batch throughput by roughly 10% compared to the expected async speedup, because workers end up retrying/serializing around the corrupted-write recovery path. This is now blocking further rollout of the async scheduler.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-50\\n\\n# Queue Design Review: Async Batch Processing — Concurrency Block\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2050\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-04 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-25)\\n\\n## Status\\n\\nT037 is **Blocked** on resolving the manifest-write race before the async scheduler can be considered production-ready; the throughput regression it causes depends directly on how the T026 worker pool's result-writing is serialized.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 50 queue design review async batch process concurr block owner bob document key doc 2050 last updat 2026 09 04 retrospect cover 2026 08 25 worker manag decis retrospect note on the concurr block confirm 2026 08 25 for larg scale redact job the batch api move from a synchron block loop to an asyncio driven queue a singl produc walk the file system and push document task while a fix pool of async worker pull from the queue and orchestr i o against the redact engin built on top of the alreadi complet multi thread worker pool t026 sourc id src gdoc 50 queue design review async batch process concurr block owner bob document key doc 2050 last updat 2026 09 04 retrospect cover 2026 08 25 order race risk becaus document vari wide in size worker finish out of order when multipl worker append to the same share result manifest concurr write can interleav and corrupt the json structur sourc id src gdoc 50 queue design review async batch process concurr block owner bob document key doc 2050 last updat 2026 09 04 retrospect cover 2026 08 25 updat confirm i o race throughput regress concurr test on 2026 08 25 confirm the race is real not just theoret under concurr load the race condit measur cut batch throughput by rough 10 compar to the expect async speedup becaus worker end up retri serial around the corrupt write recoveri path this is now block further rollout of the async schedul sourc id src gdoc 50 queue design review async batch process concurr block owner bob document key doc 2050 last updat 2026 09 04 retrospect cover 2026 08 25 status t037 is block on resolv the manifest write race befor the async schedul can be consid product readi the throughput regress it caus depend direct on how the t026 worker pool s result write is serial\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9a578b28a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-04-Async-Batch-Processing-Queue-Review.md\", \"id\": \"188f8e49d969781d\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.29613092977432864, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.12693274253475526, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6909267, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-04-Async-Batch-Processing-Queue-Review.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9a578b28a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-04-Async-Batch-Processing-Queue-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-04-Async-Batch-Processing-Queue-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1694, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:51\", \"token_count\": 573, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-44\\n\\n# Profiling Report: PDF Loader Memory Leak — Tracemalloc Patch\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2044\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-23\\n\\n## Trigger\\n\\nProfiling was opened after the T031 large-file chunking reopen surfaced memory growth on 2GB+ documents; the team wanted to confirm whether the loader itself, separate from the chunk-buffer issue being fixed under T031, was also retaining memory it shouldn't.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-44\\n\\n# Profiling Report: PDF Loader Memory Leak — Tracemalloc Patch\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2044\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-23\\n\\n## Tooling Constraint\\n\\nThe offline lab environment does not have the team's usual commercial profiler available (network-gated license check), so profiling switched to Python's stdlib `tracemalloc`, which works fully offline.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-44\\n\\n# Profiling Report: PDF Loader Memory Leak — Tracemalloc Patch\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2044\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-23\\n\\n## Findings and Patch\\n\\nTracemalloc traced the retained allocations to the PDF loader's internal page-object cache, which was holding references to fully-parsed page objects long after the redaction pass for that page had completed. Bob patched the loader to explicitly drop the cache entry once a page's redaction pass finishes, rather than waiting for document close.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-44\\n\\n# Profiling Report: PDF Loader Memory Leak — Tracemalloc Patch\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2044\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-23\\n\\n## Validation\\n\\nRe-ran the same profiling pass post-patch: peak memory during a 2GB+ document run dropped to match the chunk-bounded footprint expected from the T031 chunking work, confirming the loader-side leak — distinct from the T031 buffer-release issue — is resolved.\\n\\n*Status*: Completed. Loader-side leak patched and verified; result depends on and complements the T031 chunking/buffer-release fix.\\n\", 