aset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-25-Batch-Fail-Closed.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e961d24c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-25-Batch-Fail-Closed.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-25-Batch-Fail-Closed.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1283, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:02:50\", \"token_count\": 638, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-48\\n\\n# Evaluation Note: Electron GUI Wrapper — Package Test\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2048\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-31 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-18)\\n\\n## What Was Tested\\n\\nRetrospective note on the packaged Electron+CLI desktop build tested 2026-08-18, exercising the IPC bridge that connects the Electron frontend to the underlying batch CLI engine (T003) for a drag-and-drop batch of 100 PDFs.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-48\\n\\n# Evaluation Note: Electron GUI Wrapper — Package Test\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2048\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-31 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-18)\\n\\n## Result: Package Test Passes\\n\\nThe packaged build launches, accepts a dropped folder, invokes the batch CLI over IPC, and returns completed output files correctly. The IPC bridge to the already-completed batch CLI (T003) works as designed — this is accepted as Completed for T035 as of 2026-08-18.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-48\\n\\n# Evaluation Note: Electron GUI Wrapper — Package Test\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2048\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-31 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-18)\\n\\n## Known Rough Edge (Not Blocking)\\n\\nProgress-bar feedback during the run is uneven: because the CLI's `stdout` buffer doesn't flush at a steady cadence under heavy load (e.g., OCR-heavy pages), the UI progress indicator jumps rather than moving smoothly. This is a UX polish item, not a functional defect — the batch completes correctly regardless of how the progress bar animates.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-48\\n\\n# Evaluation Note: Electron GUI Wrapper — Package Test\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2048\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-31 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-18)\\n\\n## Possible Follow-up\\n\\nA lightweight local WebSocket channel for structured progress events (instead of `stdout` parsing) would smooth this out, but it's not required for the package test to pass and is not currently scheduled.\\n\\n*Status*: Completed. Package test passes; progress-bar smoothness is a tracked but non-blocking follow-up.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 48 evalu note electron gui wrapper packag test owner diana document key doc 2048 last updat 2026 0831 retrospect cover 2026 08 18 what wa test retrospect note on the packag electron cli desktop build test 2026 08 18 exercis the ipc bridg that connect the electron frontend to the under batch cli engin t003 for a drag and drop batch of 100 pdfs sourc id src gdoc 48 evalu note electron gui wrapper packag test owner diana document key doc 2048 last updat 2026 0831 retrospect cover 2026 08 18 result packag test pass the packag build launch accept a drop folder invok the batch cli over ipc and return complet output file correct the ipc bridg to the alreadi complet batch cli t003 work a design this is accept a complet for t035 a of 2026 08 18 sourc id src gdoc 48 evalu note electron gui wrapper packag test owner diana document key doc 2048 last updat 2026 0831 retrospect cover 2026 08 18 known rough edg not block progress bar feedback dure the run is uneven becaus the cli s stdout buffer doesn t flush at a steadi cadenc under heavi load e g ocr heavi page the ui progress indic jump rather than move smooth this is a ux polish item not a function defect the batch complet correct regardless of how